{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLqKnB5GrhMUQENY7HRm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: `limit(2**(1/x), x, 0, dir='-')` now returns `0`, which is correct. The limit and gruntz test files pass (211 passed, 3 skipped, 6 expected failures).\n\n**Cause:** In `sympy/series/limits.py`, `Limit.doit` falls back on a helper, `pow_heuristics`, for powers like `b**f(x)`. That helper works out smaller limits (for example, the limit of `e1*log(b1)`) but never passed the direction along, so they always used the default `dir='+'`. For `2**(1/x)` as x→0⁻, it took the limit of `log(2)/x` from the right, got `+oo`, and returned `exp(oo) = oo`.\n\n**Fix:** `pow_heuristics` now takes a `dir` argument, passes it to all four of its inner `limit` calls, and the one place that calls it supplies it. That's 6 lines changed, all in that file.\n\n**Results after the fix:**\n- `limit(2**(1/x), x, 0, '-')` → `0`\n- `limit(2**(1/x), x, 0, '+')` → `oo` (unchanged)\n- `limit(2**x, x, -oo)` → `0`\n- `limit((1/2)**x, x, -oo)` → `oo`\n- `limit((1+x)**(1/x), x, 0, '-')` → `E`\n\nOne note on your second example: `limit(2**x, x, -oo)` already returned `0` in this checkout before my change. So that part of the issue seems to be fixed already here, or reached by a different code path than in 1.13.3. Only the one-sided limit at 0 was still wrong."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":268,"cache_read_input_tokens":23167,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":268},"output_tokens":552,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d53b818-669a-4406-be15-f180237d93e0","uuid":"b089ef17-3cee-4d13-8f98-d3450617d004","timestamp":"2026-11-24T00:49:28.775Z","requ