t, got `+oo`, and returned `exp(oo) = oo`.\n\n**Fix:** `pow_heuristics` now takes a `dir` argument, passes it to all four of its inner `limit` calls, and the one place that calls it supplies it. That's 6 lines changed, all in that file.\n\n**Results after the fix:**\n- `limit(2**(1/x), x, 0, '-')` → `0`\n- `limit(2**(1/x), x, 0, '+')` → `oo` (unchanged)\n- `limit(2**x, x, -oo)` → `0`\n- `limit((1/2)**x, x, -oo)` → `oo`\n- `limit((1+x)**(1/x), x, 0, '-')` → `E`\n\nOne note on your second example: `limit(2**x, x, -oo)` already returned `0` in this checkout before my change. So that part of the issue seems to be fixed already here, or reached by a different code path than in 1.13.3. Only the one-sided limit at 0 was still wrong.","ttft_ms":6059,"type":"result","duration_ms":102236,"uuid":"eb870654-9708-479d-9050-6cda7b810eb9","ttft_stream_ms":4301,"time_to_request_ms":54,"first_content_frame_ms":4301,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":16,"outputTokens":2802,"cacheReadInputTokens":151172,"cacheCreationInputTokens":14761,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2044264,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":298,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":14761,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
